+Results of the four rows above (MetalSim, M4 Max; integrated `2ed5219a` -> this branch, newton `metalsim-integrated-2`):
+G1 MuJoCo Warp at 4,096 worlds (`g1_tp_variants.py`, two interleaved runs): flat physics 47.1 -> 46.2 ms per step, env step 109.1 / 108.4 -> 92.8 / 92.8, rollout + inference 101.1 / 101.3 -> 99.3 / 99.6 ms per step, full PPO loop 38.3k / 38.1k -> 38.9k / 38.8k env-steps/s; rough physics 70.8 -> 69.5 / 69.3, env step 118.8 / 119.4 -> 104.4 / 104.4, rollout 114.8 / 114.5 -> 112.7 / 112.9, loop 32.2k / 32.3k -> 32.8k / 32.7k (constant arguments everywhere, `WP_METAL_DEVICE_ARGS=0`: physics 47.1 / 70.8, as the integrated tree).
+MPM ms per frame (`speed_bench.py`, 60 frames, two interleaved runs; device arguments as `newton_compat.install` sets them / Warp's "auto"): granular 33.98 -> 31.62 / 31.70, multi_material 37.61 -> 35.38 / 35.48, two-way 67.35 -> 58.34 / 57.95, two-way captured 40.70 -> 39.58 / 39.24, ANYmal 42.78 -> 36.80 / 37.70, ANYmal captured 31.34 -> 27.56 / 27.33, plate drag 30.86 -> 30.41 / 30.30, column a = 8 25.26 -> 25.43 / 25.30, column a = 2 18.94 -> 18.48 / 18.84. The six floor recordings (granular, multi_material, two-way, ANYmal, plate drag, column a = 2) are bitwise those of the integrated tree.
