+| `3c4e251e` | `warp.fem` dispatched assembly takes CUDA's tiling choice on Metal. For long quadratures, CUDA sums each node's contributions in 32 lanes (strided lane sums, then the shuffle tree of `tile_sum`). The heuristic in `_generate_auxiliary_kernels` was CUDA-only, so Metal summed them sequentially. That is a different rounding of every particle-to-grid sum in Newton's implicit MPM: after one step of `example_mpm_multi_material`, 72 % of the nodes differed from the L4 by up to 10 ulp. Metal's SIMD-group reduction is the CUDA shuffle tree, so node mass and momentum now equal the L4's bit for bit. The tiling decisions of MetalSim's six floor scenes equal the L4's call for call. |
