+Raise at launch on Metal for 64-bit `wp.atomic_cas()` / `wp.atomic_exch()` and signed 64-bit `wp.atomic_min()` / `wp.atomic_max()`, which Apple GPUs cannot perform atomically, instead of running them as a plain read-modify-write; make 64-bit `wp.atomic_and()` / `wp.atomic_or()` / `wp.atomic_xor()` and shared-tile int64 additions exact on Metal.
diff --git a/changelog/+metal-bounded-launch.added.md b/changelog/+metal-bounded-launch.added.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..13119db7e7d8879c1b587ae7e71c809966544df3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/+metal-bounded-launch.added.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+Add `wp.launch(..., dim_limit=...)`: a 1-element `int32` device array that bounds the first launch dimension.
+Tasks past the bound may be skipped, so fixed-capacity buffers whose used part is only known on the device can be
+processed without host synchronization. On Metal only the threadgroups below the bound are dispatched (an
+indirect dispatch sized on the GPU, also inside captured graphs and indirect execution ranges); other devices
+run the full `dim`. `warp.config.metal_bounded_launch` (`WP_METAL_BOUNDED_LAUNCH=0`) turns it off.
